## 1. ✶ Observe — standing ground

**MEASURED.** `I1` follows the sealed anchor; Wave C, K15-H and Wave D landed ([road:487,459](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem)). No production `@intents-` plane surfaced in the code search. The carrier already names five planes, while the current derivation and ring enumerate four ([persona-scope.ts:121](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-scope.ts), [persona-group-ring.ts:136](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts)). The shared HMAC tag derives from the PersonaGroup ID; one bag name follows each relation ([persona-scope.ts:81](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-scope.ts)). Founding creates plane documents and bootstrap entries; a `plane` act in signed `@persona` must vouch for each URL before registration. The verifier re-derives canonical bytes, checks Ed25519 and authorizes against face anchor/KEL; the projector admits only URLs backed by those acts ([init.ts:129](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/commands/init.ts), [signed-act.ts:2](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/signed-act.ts), [persona-act.ts:96](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-act.ts)). Node registers all proven held planes and mounts the worn face; browser registers after face proof ([open-node-vessel.ts:2200](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts), [open-browser-vessel.ts:1181](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts)). The ring lets each face's own devices sync governed documents ([persona-group-ring.ts:136](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts)); the herm carries without opening them. Wave D seals atom and anchor as separate face custody rows under each face's FCK; the plane itself retains its distinct rest/wire seal rules ([k15-wave-d-lane.mem:33](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem), [plane-seal.ts:5](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/plane-seal.ts)).

**MEASURED.** Node loads the worn face's atom from custody; browser derives its atom key from that face's seed. The device seed serves substrate duties; the atom signs face proof and face acts ([open-node-vessel.ts:1887](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts), [open-browser-vessel.ts:686](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts), [open-browser-vessel.ts:861](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts)). Today a remote summons lands in the daemon Automerge doc, each daemon dispatcher converts it to local volatile invocation, tombstones transport, and writes an outcome back to the daemon doc; each vessel runs its own daemon VM ([verb-dispatcher.ts:1](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-dispatcher.ts)). `face-join` runs there, rejects joinee self-seating, then records its grant on `@persona`; two hearths can still re-key before either sees an outcome ([operator-daemon-behavior.ts:601](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts), [face-join.ts:189](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-join.ts)). Reactors register in the daemon island, sometimes posting pool work to main; browser composes the same island/dispatcher. The CLI names a face per invocation ([operator-daemon-behavior.ts:371](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts), [daemon-behavior.ts:182](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-behavior.ts), [CHANGELOG.md:17](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/CHANGELOG.md)).

## 3. ⏿ Orient — red-first lane slices

**LEAD.** One I1 lane should carry a single wire image and node/browser parity through the summons cutover; place relay research and build in a later lane. Each red below needs its named passing control.

1. **Plane and image:** red: two faces cross-read, a late joinee misses the plane, unsigned URL registers, or plane projects; controls: same-face sync, signed URL registration, projected wiki file. Hold `persona-scope`, `register-bags`, `persona-group-ring`, founding/admit bundles, signed act/projector, node/browser openers, seal and mirror guards.
2. **Execution:** red: prior outcome still triggers effect; wrong pinned atom acts; class-addressed single-effect issues. Controls: fresh intent acts; matching pinned atom acts. Hold shared `intent-plane`/verb policy and both daemon composers/dispatcher bridges.
3. **Fold:** red: partitioned idempotent duplicate, replay with same nonce, `every` reduced to one slot, claim zombie after takeover, injected clock read. Controls: fresh nonce changes ID; fenced current claimant acts; one outcome per `every` device. Hold shared image/verifier/fold plus effect adapters.
4. **Void and join:** red: sleeping device acts after observed cancel/revocation/roster edge; two hearths re-key one joinee. Controls: unbounded intent acts; one hearth grants and second stands down; CLI-selected face reaches its own plane. Hold face-join, operation store, daemon behavior and node/browser join bridges.
5. **Read pane and rubric:** red: pane writes through, keystrokes/save emit intent, duplicate-answer counter silently reads zero. Controls: committed move emits one intent/outcome; seeded duplicate trips counter; projected wiki still mirrors while intent plane does not. Hold daemon wiki view, UI bridge and instrumentation.

**MEASURED overlap.** W14–W16 touch `place-floor-pin`, `admit-gate-pin`, card filing and `nexus-contract`; K17 touches frontier/lease/realm boards; W26 slice 5 touches a sealed floor accept row per (face, Nexus) ([road:512](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem), [road:515](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem)). I1 should consume their verified frontier/face readers and avoid editing those files; a shared composer hunk needs one owner at integration. Their signed acts never substitute for intent outcomes.

## 2. ◇ Decide — model joints

**Canon rules:** the carrier explicitly orders `intent/outcome/asks/answer/claim/release/takeover/supersede/cancel`, four audience modes, hash of issuer/verb/arguments/nonce, empty nonce for idempotent verbs, outcome cause/signer, preference winner then lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, no timed expiry, operator release priority, causal voids, late `every` membership, and single-effect refusal for class/any-device ([carrier:47–92](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem)). A duplicate winner changes the read, never undoes an effect. House law **no global now** forbids timestamp arbitration; **one name, one relation** calls for one shared image; **isomorphic by intent** calls for one fold on both hosts. The rubric rules cross-device, settled, answerable authority decisions and excludes bodies, keystrokes and ordinary wiki saves; the pane reads only ([carrier:111–139](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem)).

**Operator-owned choices, with leans:** (a) Does `answer` assigning an executor replace an invalid unpinned single-effect intent, or only complete an `asks` gate? Lean: require an explicit ask and bind the answer to its ID before execution. (b) Which signed canonical envelope and content hash version binds all kinds, and how do concurrent cancel/takeover/release fold? Lean: domain-separated canonical signed entries with stable IDs, per-intent causal references, authority-first release; never arrival order. (c) What fences an irreversible face-join re-key before outcome visibility? Lean: pinned hearth or preference order plus operation ID checked at the Keyhive effect door; outcome stand-down alone cannot prevent partitioned double action. (d) Does `every` mean joined devices at issue or all later joins until causal bound? Canon selects later joins; decide a bounded roster edge for finite campaigns. (e) How does the view expose duplicate, void-after-act and unknown frontier? Lean: show all, label counted outcome, never hide conflict. These decisions need operator ruling before slice 1 freezes the image.

## 4. ▶ Act — prior art and stories

**MEASURED outside.** [Automerge sync](https://automerge.org/docs/tutorial/local-sync/) and [local-first doctrine](https://www.inkandswitch.com/essay/local-first/) support offline replica convergence; [Keyhive/Beelay](https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/blob/main/README.md) supplies signed delegation and authorized sync. [OTP supervisors](https://www.erlang.org/doc/system/sup_princ.html) restart local workers, while [actor mailboxes](https://www.erlang.org/doc/system/ref_man_processes.html) serialize one actor's intake; neither guarantees one fleet-wide effect. [Patchwork tasks](https://www.inkandswitch.com/patchwork/notebook/tasks-01/) show CRDT-carried work; the intent/outcome fold still needs application semantics. [Kubernetes leader election](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election/) uses renew time, duration and a central compare-and-swap. **LEAD:** this house substitutes signed causal bounds, audience slots, idempotent effects and explicit takeover, never a clock lease.

**Gaia.** Laptop commits “rebuild the wiki” as one intent while phone sleeps. Laptop acts and signs outcome; phone wakes, syncs, sees its slot answered and stands down. If both acted under partition, their idempotency key converges and both receipts remain visible.

**Elyncia.** Two shrine hearths see one keeper-face join summons. A pinned hearth seats the joinee; the second reads the outcome and stands down. If the first vanishes, a human release/answer redirects through a signed causal act; no sunset clock grants the second permission.

## ↺ Hoʻoko / aftermath

**LEAD:** Rule the five choices above, then cut the red-first lane. Repo inspection only; no suites ran. Next observation should verify the signed image against the live floor/frontier integration head.

