bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:33:''The Council's lease never runs backward.'' A stale replica of the Council's daemon doc arrives missing the newest lease slot. Before Wave C, an old device edge reads current against it. After it, each device keeps a sealed frontier that never falls, and the stale replica moves nothing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:47:# ''The sealed anchor.'' Each face holds, on each device, a D row: its PersonaGroup, persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Founding, admission and the recovery rites write it; sync never does. Red: a forged selector row in the daemon doc, then a coherent valid foreign bundle, switch no pinned face; a missing anchor refuses face boot by name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:49:# ''The monotone frontier.'' Lease advances carry signatures in the per-writer shape (`lease-advance`: each writer signs `{resource, writer, epoch}` into its own slot); the sealed local frontier never falls. A lease advance rides a per-writer signed slot and never the `@persona` log, since two writers advancing at once would fork a hash-linked log, and the house names forks and never resolves them; per-writer slots let concurrent writers both land while the max climbs. A face's advance is `lares persona lease`, and the boot raises the anchor only from slots that verify (`lease-observation`). Red: a deleted, replayed or unsigned high slot lowers nothing and raises nothing. An act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) refuses a target naming a newer bound than the frontier holds, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:51:# ''The FCK fence.'' Each face's D rows (atom, archive, anchor, custody root, proof keys) seal under that face's own random FCK and key by its PersonaGroup on both hosts; the vessel key opens none of them. Red: K15's isolation red at the key-class level, where Wave B's `test.fails` rows turn green: unlock A alone, and every key A holds, the vessel key included, opens no B row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:53:# ''One SharedWorker per house.'' A tab knows its face from its custody anchor before it connects, then opens the SharedWorker whose `name` digests that house's (PersonaGroup, persona root); the house's island runs in that worker's own thread and realm, with no nested Worker (Chromium exposes none inside a SharedWorker), so each face keeps its own realm, one island per house, and a house outlives any one of its tabs. Red, in a real browser on every engine: two faces' tabs reach two worker instances, a second tab of one face reaches the same one, and the last tab's close ends the house.
